{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BuUCdLvXjma3N1WYyZqJeq","type":"tool_result","content":"        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n--\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"start\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n--","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2389841-42ad-481f-ae69-21915de2c51d","uuid":"df77bb92-22c1-4404-bfb5-5c5b5791962a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:30:01.425Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n--\n            \"hr\": {\n              \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n              \"start\": 88,\n              \"end\": 93\n            },\n--","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-29A32f/gen.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":7,"newStart":10,"newLines":12,"lines":[" def hr_target(step):","     \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"","     lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]","-    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}","+    # Intervals reads a corridor as start/end. \"value\" means a single target,","+    # which the Garmin export turns into a watch HR zone number (so the watch","+    # shows its own zone band and \"end\" is ignored).","+    if lo == hi:","+        return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo}","+    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}"," "," "," def build_step(step):"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-29A32f/gen.py"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BuUCdLvXjma3N1WYyZqJeq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAotAYdjLFmnMi42iAkS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ECFfgZbLXca1brTFMAVM5i","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-29A32f/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n`gen.py` wrote each HR corridor as\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 68, \"end\": 75}\n```\n\nIn an Intervals.icu `workout_doc` step, a range is written as `start` + `end`.\n`value` means a single target. Intervals took the step as a single %LTHR\ntarget and ignored `end`. When it exports a single HR target to Garmin, it\nsends a **zone number** instead of a bpm range. The watch then shows its own\nband for that zone. This matches every symptom in `readback/watch-notes.md`:\n\n- Each step shows exactly one of the watch's zone bands (Warm-up → Z2,\n  Tempo → Z4, Float → Z3, Cool-down → Z2).\n- Changing the watch's LTHR moves the bands, but the targets stay on zone\n  edges. The watch is resolving a zone number against its own zones.\n- The API returned the doc unchanged, so nothing was rejected. The field was\n  just read differently from what we meant.\n\nThe two earlier workarounds were wrong for separate reasons. `\"bpm\"` is not\nan HR unit, and values like 125–145 read as %LTHR give 214–249. And\n`start_bpm`/`end_bpm` are fields Intervals computes, not inputs.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`, `hr_target`)\n- Corridors are now written as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n  Intervals keeps them as %LTHR, converts them to bpm with the athlete's LTHR\n  (172) at export, and sends them as a custom HR range.\n- If a plan gives the same low and high value, the generator writes a single\n  `value` target, which is the correct form for that case.\n\nPlans and `push.sh` are unchanged. The README is still accurate (HR targets\nare %LTHR and Intervals converts them).\n\n## Not done / to verify\nI did not push anything (no external calls). To confirm, regenerate and push\n(`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`),\nthen sync. The watch should show roughly 117–129, 151–160, 129–141 and\n112–124 bpm. You may want to delete event 184233 first so the old version\ndoesn't stay on the calendar.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1603,"cache_read_input_tokens":22160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1603},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2389841-42ad-481f-ae69-21915de2c51d","uuid":"b5dc96b2-7d1c-4201-aa91-a916fde254a5","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:30:11.573Z","request_id":"req_011CgAotAAZh4CdNariL26jG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01ECFfgZbLXca1brTFMAVM5i":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-29A32f/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n`gen.py` wrote each HR corridor as\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 68, \"end\": 75}\n```\n\nIn an Intervals.icu `workout_doc` step, a range is written as `start` + `end`.\n`value` means a single target. Intervals took the step as a single %LTHR\ntarget and ignored `end`. When it exports a single HR target to Garmin, it\nsends a **zone number** instead of a bpm range. The watch then shows its own\nband for that zone. This matches every symptom in `readback/watch-notes.md`:\n\n- Each step shows exactly one of the watch's zone bands (Warm-up → Z2,\n  Tempo → Z4, Float → Z3, Cool-down → Z2).\n- Changing the watch's LTHR moves the bands, but the targets stay on zone\n  edges. The watch is resolving a zone number against its own zones.\n- The API returned the doc unchanged, so nothing was rejected. The field was\n  just read differently from what we meant.\n\nThe two earlier workarounds were wrong for separate reasons. `\"bpm\"` is not\nan HR unit, and values like 125–145 read as %LTHR give 214–249. And\n`start_bpm`/`end_bpm` are fields Intervals computes, not inputs.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`, `hr_target`)\n- Corridors are now written as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n  Intervals keeps them as %LTHR, converts them to bpm with the athlete's LTHR\n  (172) at export, and sends them as a custom HR range.\n- If a plan gives the same low and high value, the generator writes a single\n  `value` target, which is the correct form for that case.\n\nPlans and `push.sh` are unchanged. The README is still accurate (HR targets\nare %LTHR and Intervals converts them).\n\n## Not done / to verify\nI did not push anything (no external calls). To confirm, regenerate and push\n(`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`),\nthen sync. The watch should show roughly 117–129, 151–160, 129–141 and\n112–124 bpm. You may want to delete event 184233 first so the old version\ndoesn't stay on the calendar.\n"}}}
